{"animath":"0.1","kind":"concept","title":"Reproduction: pollination to seed","level":"secondary","subject":"science","topic":"bio-reproduction","canvas":{"width":960,"height":540},"scenes":[{"id":"s1","caption":"Pollination: pollen on the move","duration_ms":10000,"narration":"Pollination is the delivery step: pollen grains travel from one flower's anther to another flower's stigma. Wind, water, and animals all help.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","explain":"Scene: pollination, pollen on the move. Hover to see how pollen travels.","kind":"text","text":"Pollination: pollen on the move","x":80,"y":70,"size":34}},{"at_ms":600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fA","explain":"Flower A: the source flower. Pollen travels from its anther.","kind":"circle","cx":270,"cy":320,"r":75,"fill":"#ffe3ef","stroke":"#d1478a","strokeWidth":4}},{"at_ms":1000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fAL","explain":"Label: Flower A.","kind":"text","x":232,"y":328,"size":26,"text":"flower A"}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fB","explain":"Flower B: the receiving flower. Pollen lands on its stigma.","kind":"circle","cx":700,"cy":320,"r":75,"fill":"#ffe3ef","stroke":"#d1478a","strokeWidth":4}},{"at_ms":1800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fBL","explain":"Label: Flower B.","kind":"text","x":662,"y":328,"size":26,"text":"flower B"}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pA1","explain":"A pollen grain: the tiny package that carries the male part of the plant.","kind":"circle","cx":252,"cy":278,"r":10,"fill":"#f2c94c","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":2400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pA2","explain":"A pollen grain: the tiny package that carries the male part of the plant.","kind":"circle","cx":288,"cy":272,"r":10,"fill":"#f2c94c","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":2600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pA3","explain":"A pollen grain: the tiny package that carries the male part of the plant.","kind":"circle","cx":270,"cy":252,"r":10,"fill":"#f2c94c","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":3000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"carrierB","explain":"A pollinator: an animal helping carry pollen from flower A to flower B.","kind":"circle","cx":270,"cy":200,"r":14,"fill":"#8a5a2b","stroke":"#5c3a1a","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"move","dur_ms":1100,"target":"carrierB","to":{"cx":480,"cy":215}},{"at_ms":4500,"do":"move","dur_ms":1100,"target":"carrierB","to":{"cx":700,"cy":215}},{"at_ms":5600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pollenB1","explain":"A pollen grain carried to flower B.","kind":"circle","cx":610,"cy":240,"r":10,"fill":"#f2c94c","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":5800,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"pollenB1","to":{"cx":690,"cy":262}},{"at_ms":6600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pollenB2","explain":"A pollen grain carried to flower B.","kind":"circle","cx":600,"cy":270,"r":10,"fill":"#f2c94c","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":6800,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"pollenB2","to":{"cx":700,"cy":285}},{"at_ms":7600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"t1","explain":"A note: pollination means pollen transfer. Delivery, not fusion.","kind":"text","x":380,"y":180,"size":24,"text":"pollination = pollen transfer"}},{"at_ms":8600,"do":"caption","text":"A grain of pollen lands on another flower's stigma."}]},{"id":"s2","caption":"Fertilisation: tube to ovule","duration_ms":11000,"narration":"Once pollen lands, it grows a tube down the style. The male nucleus travels through the tube and fuses with the ovule.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","explain":"Scene: fertilisation, from tube to ovule. Hover to follow the male nucleus.","kind":"text","text":"Fertilisation: tube to ovule","x":80,"y":70,"size":34}},{"at_ms":600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"stigma","explain":"The stigma: the sticky landing pad where pollen grains land.","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":160,"r":28,"fill":"#f5c6e0","stroke":"#d1478a","strokeWidth":3}},{"at_ms":1000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"stigmaL","explain":"Label: Stigma.","kind":"text","x":425,"y":168,"size":22,"text":"stigma"}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"style","explain":"The style: the stalk the pollen tube grows down.","kind":"rect","x":362,"y":192,"w":36,"h":120,"fill":"#bfe3b4","stroke":"#2e8b57","strokeWidth":3}},{"at_ms":1800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"styleL","explain":"Label: Style.","kind":"text","x":410,"y":255,"size":22,"text":"style"}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ovary","explain":"The ovary: it holds the ovules.","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":385,"r":55,"fill":"#ffe3ef","stroke":"#d1478a","strokeWidth":3}},{"at_ms":2600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ovaryL","explain":"Label: Ovary.","kind":"text","x":445,"y":392,"size":22,"text":"ovary"}},{"at_ms":3000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ovule","explain":"The ovule: the female part that fuses with the male nucleus.","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":410,"r":20,"fill":"#fff3b0","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":3}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"grain","explain":"A pollen grain: once landed, it grows a tube down the style.","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":118,"r":12,"fill":"#f2c94c","stroke":"#b8860b","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":3800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tube","explain":"The pollen tube: it grows down the style, carrying the male nucleus.","kind":"arrow","x1":380,"y1":150,"x2":380,"y2":190,"stroke":"#2e8b57","width":5}},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"tube","to":{"x2":380,"y2":255}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"tube","to":{"x2":380,"y2":320}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"tube","to":{"x2":380,"y2":395}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"nucleus","explain":"The male nucleus: it travels through the pollen tube to the ovule.","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":180,"r":9,"fill":"#c0392b","stroke":"#7c1f14","strokeWidth":2}},{"at_ms":7400,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"nucleus","to":{"cx":380,"cy":250}},{"at_ms":8200,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"nucleus","to":{"cx":380,"cy":320}},{"at_ms":900